@@ -6,4 +6,6 @@
 
 The function returns a list of at most `limit` products, best first, each with `id`, `name`, `price`, `rating` and `reason` (one line of at most 80 characters, shown under the product). Only products that exist in the catalogue and are in stock are returned, each one once. A blank search, or a catalogue with nothing in stock, gives an empty list.
 
+The reason is written by the model, so it is checked before it is returned: a price or bound ("under 100"), a rating ("4.9/5") or a standing ("cheapest", "top-rated", "cheap") that disagrees with the product's own figures, or with the other products in the returned list, makes the reason empty. Comparisons that cannot be checked ("cheaper than the others", "best value") are treated the same way. Numbers that are not prices or ratings ("30 hour battery", "1 m") are left alone.
+
 Run the tests with `python -m unittest` from this directory.
